WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.480
You're incredibly lucky.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.180
That went well.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.990
Anyway, were you serious about there 
being an overnight trip this weekend?

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.610
Yeah. I just heard about it, too.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.650
Everyone on the student council is going.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.320
Where?

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.240
Kusatsu.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.070
And you're going to the hot springs?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.830
That means Rina-senpai's going, right?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.400
So you're going to the hot springs
with Rina-senpai!

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.250
So <i>anything</i> could happen between you?!

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.850
What are you talking about?

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.710
It's just a student council...

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.630
On second thought,
anything <i>could</i> happen, yes.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.550
Aw, jeez.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.640
Why do good things keep happening to you?

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.140
You're incredibly unlucky.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.930
Itsuki, at the very least...

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.730
At the very least, could you tell me

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.310
what's happening on the trip 
while we play <i>PSO2</i> at night?

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.890
In great detail, please.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.390
What are you going to do with 
such detailed information?

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.530
Don't ask.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.290
Kusatsu Onsen Bus Terminal

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.350
It's quite amazing that we're splurging
on a hot springs trip.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:22.560
<b>The Original Hahaya</b>

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.090
The student council goes 
on a trip every year.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.560
Every year, huh?

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.900
We go under the pretext of holding meetings,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.090
but it's primarily meant to be recreational.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.810
Come to think of it, where's Suzuki-san?

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.820
She said she had something
important to do today.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.930
I don't have time for your games.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.700
I'm sorry.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.790
This place is awesome.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.290
Welcome.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.350
We're the Seiga Academy Student Council. 
We made reservations the other day.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.760
Thank you for coming.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.340
We've been expecting you.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.670
Yumiko-san and Last Samurai-san?

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.850
Hello. Thanks for the other day.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.770
No, thank you.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.350
Does that mean...

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.710
The two of them operate this hot springs inn.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.350
Really?

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.310
You must be exhausted.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.860
Let me show you to your room.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.910
Itsuki-kun, want to play <i>PSO2</i> tonight?

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.590
Great idea.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.790
No.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.160
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.550
He's not allowed to play <i>PSO2</i> for a while.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.840
He's been skipping work to play it recently.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.250
I told you, I feel like I 
suddenly got better recently.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.480
And Itsuki-kun's here today. 
Let me at least play a little.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.710
No.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.470
<b>Kiri Room</b>

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.470
This is your room.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.390
Make yourselves at home.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:52.030
Yumiko-san is surprisingly strict.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:56.670
I can't imagine a life without <i>PSO2</i> right now.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.130
You, too.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:58.990
What?

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.330
No <i>PSO2</i>.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.960
Jinbaya

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.960
No <i>PSO2</i>?

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.330
<b>Quest 06      Forbidden PSO2</b>

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.760
Wait, why?

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.170
Just because.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.550
That concludes my report on online games.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.280
Any questions?

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:51.090
You're not concerned online games could 
have a negative effect on academics?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.810
No.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.270
In fact, Tachibana Itsuki-kun,
the student council vice president,

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.460
is currently responsible for writing 
reports while playing <i>PSO2</i>,

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.000
and his grades are excellent.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.570
About this Tachibana-kun...

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.570
His grades don't look so excellent to me.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.080
Uh, there's a reason for this.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:18.830
I've been doing really well at <i>PSO2</i> lately.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.590
It's been getting more fun,

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.220
so I sort of forget to study.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.810
It's like I've crossed a line or I'm 
on an endless adventure or something.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.700
In other words, <i>PSO2</i> is just that fun.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:37.040
Didn't I tell you from the start 
that you can't let your grades drop?

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.850
Yes.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.720
You need to get your grades back up
with the upcoming midterm exams.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.860
Until then, you can't play <i>PSO2</i>.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.120
No way!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.490
That concludes today's meeting.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.290
Thanks.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.750
Thanks.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.120
Did you record the minutes?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.370
Perfectly.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.750
We still have some time before dinner.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.000
You're free to use that time as you please.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.410
Okay.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.130
Then I'm taking a bath.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.060
Uh, what is this?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:13.340
Finish all of these
by the end of the trip.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:14.370
Got it?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.390
<i>A-All</i> of these?

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:18.750
Got it?

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.650
Okay.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.420
A hot springs trip isn't complete 
without playing ping pong.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.900
Sasaki-kun, want to play?

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.100
You sure?

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.170
Why not?

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:53.780
Why do I have to do this when 
we came all the way to Kusatsu?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.680
Working hard?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.240
I guess.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.570
That's a lot of problems, though.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.940
I can't finish all of these today.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.420
Besides, don't you think it's weird?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.560
Rina-senpai's the one who 
told me to play <i>PSO2</i>,

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.490
and now she's telling me not to play.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.360
Fantastic.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:15.950
What?

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.330
This problem set.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.440
It covers all the important points.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.830
It's well written.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.580
I see.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.430
Kudo-senpai, are your grades okay?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.410
Of course.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:33.340
I'm a student council officer, 
and I always rank high on all my tests.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.350
If anything, this is more difficult for me.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:41.050
The game does get harder
as you complete more quests.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.450
That's not the kind of quest
I'm talking about.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.100
What?

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:48.000
I have a friend who refuses to meet me IRL,
no matter how much I invite them.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.300
I see.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:55.580
Today's the day I'll get you, 
my pretty little OrgaCats-chan!

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.120
OrgaCats?

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.470
Did you see that, you scrub?

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.260
Stare...

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.230
I'm sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.320
It's just like <i>PSO2</i>.

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:24.730
Your true nature comes out.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.980
No, this isn't my true nature.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:31.600
Ma'am.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.110
What is it?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.610
Want to take a bath together?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.840
Sorry. I need to finish this first.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:38.620
I'll help you!

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.420
It's all right.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.750
Since we came all the way here, 
you should enjoy the baths.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:08:59.650
What?

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.750
Uh, nothing.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.430
Konoe-san, you play <i>PSO2</i>, too?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.520
Is that a problem?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.160
No, I just thought that was cute.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.520
It really brings out your personality.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.730
I thought it was charming.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:12.830
Well, yeah.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.120
Hey, wait. Hurry up and do your problems!

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.280
O-Okay.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:21.880
Hold on.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:22.630
What?

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:27.140
Were you commenting on my body?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:27.970
What?

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.540
No, that's not what I meant.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.050
Are you trying to say I have a childish body?

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.770
No, no.

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.800
Better do my problem set.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.480
Why is the president so interested in you?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.360
What? Rina-senpai is?

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:47.940
I don't think she's only interested in me.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.120
She wrote that problem set
you're doing, you know.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:52.860
What?

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.450
She's busy enough with her 
student council duties.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.350
I'll help.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:00.450
Thanks.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.080
But I'm the one who invited 
Tachibana-kun to play <i>PSO2</i>.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.930
I'm also responsible for 
the drop in his grades.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.810
Now that I think about it,

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:19.470
my grades dropping isn't 
anyone's fault but mine.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.060
What? You just realized that?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.220
I can't accept this.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.880
Why does the president 
care about him so much?

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.430
Let's eat.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.070
Thanks for the food.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.130
Tachibana-kun?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.360
You're already finished?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.680
But the food...

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.820
You should've savored it more.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.950
My time is limited.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.120
He's working really hard.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.210
He's just being stubborn.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:37.130
<b>[Item Lab]</b> A facility that allows players to upgrade their weapons and equipment. Upgrading items has a chance of failure, but the often irritating remarks of Dudu, one of the Item Lab's NPCs, makes him the target of players' rage when they fail to upgrade their items, and he is even known as the “real final boss” of <i>PSO2</i>.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:41.760
<b>[Quests]</b> Descending onto target planets to complete missions. Quests including a variety of activities such as defeating certain enemies or defending certain points, but they are widely divided into permanent quests that can be accepted at any time and emergency quests that suddenly appear and can only be accepted in a limited time frame.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.260
Jinbaya

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.760
<b>Kiri Room</b>

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.100
Sword Hunt

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.730
I'm finished.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.840
Ouch, my hips...

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.820
I should take a bath before I go to bed.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:11.140
Itsuki-kun.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.500
Last Samurai-san?

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.870
What is it?

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.120
Are you going to the baths?

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:22.220
Yeah. It's a bit late, 
but I can still go, right?

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:25.470
In that case, you should 
try the outdoor bath.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.220
The outdoor bath?

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:32.140
It's in the annex, so not 
many guests go there.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.070
I see.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:34.980
Well, excuse me.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:46.060
This feels great.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:52.580
What's that?

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:02.130
<b>Let us play PSO2
together tonight!
- Last Samurai</b>

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.730
<i>Let us play </i>PSO2<i> together tonight!</i>

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.130
<i>- Last Samurai.</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.760
I appreciate the thought, but...

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.600
You need to get your grades back up
with the upcoming midterm exams.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.760
Until then, you can't play <i>PSO2</i>.

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.300
Just one quest...

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.270
No, a promise is a promise.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:19.780
Koa.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.500
I've been waiting for you.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.520
Enjoying the hot springs?

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.900
The outdoor bath is nice.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.910
So you're playing <i>PSO2</i> from an outdoor bath?

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.220
Yeah, but sorry.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.720
I can't quest tonight.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:35.170
What? Why not?

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.160
Well, actually...

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.880
Something happened at the 
hot springs, didn't it?

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:39.800
What happened?

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.970
Tell me! Tell me all the details!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.130
Nothing like what you're thinking happened.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.300
Liar!

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.260
It's true.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:49.820
Huh?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.740
Huh? What? What?

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:52.760
Itsuki?

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.730
Why are you coming in here?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.950
Hey, what's up?

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:57.180
I'll talk to you later.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.100
W-Wait, Suzuki-san.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.400
Wh-Why?

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:11.070
I finished my mission earlier than expected.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.920
R-Really?

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:17.460
You finished early, so you came here?

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.760
Wait, that's not important! 
This is the men's bath!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.320
Why are you so flustered?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:31.420
Judging by Itsuki's behavior, 
someone else must have entered the bath.

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:33.480
And at this moment,

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.480
he's undoubtedly experiencing...

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.770
...something delightful!

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:48.790
Sorry for using your kitchen 
in the middle of the night.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.280
It's fine.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.950
Must be nice to have such a cute girlfriend
make a midnight snack for you.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.290
Itsuki-kun's a lucky, lucky boy.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.290
Actually, it's not like that.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.440
Oh, are you going somewhere?

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.800
Uh, yeah.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:09.050
I'm just going out for a 
drink in the night air.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.360
You're not thinking

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:15.220
about playing <i>PSO2</i> just because 
you're done with work, are you?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.060
Yeah, right.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.910
Tachibana-kun, are you hanging in there?

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.300
I thought he was studying.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.260
Did he run away?

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:51.550
He finished everything in 
such a short amount of time?

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.450
He did work hard.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.900
But where did he go?

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:00.060
He must be hiding somewhere and...

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.850
He's not logged in.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.320
<b>Friend List
Group Order
Character Name/Player ID Name Block/Location
Online (5)
Koa
Silver
Kid
OrgaCats
Master Nezumi
Offline
 (4)Itsuki
Last Samurai</b>

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.950
Itsuki's in an outdoor bath right now.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.820
Boy, that sounds fun.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:26.170
I guess I'll try to enjoy 
some hot springs in <i>PSO2</i>.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:37.100
<b>Koa? I want to talk. 
Do you have a minute?</b>

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.540
<i>Koa? I want to talk.</i>

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:32.860
<i>Do you have a minute?</i>

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:35.790
Rina-senpai?

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:41.620
Yes. I am currently bathing 
at the hot springs.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.350
We can speak here if that's 
all right with you.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.440
<b>Okay.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:46.440
<i>Okay. I'll be right there.</i>

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.700
What? Rina-san is coming here?

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:53.210
Wait, a bath?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.650
I'm going to share a bath with Rina-san?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:55.690
Seriously?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.280
Boy, it never hurts to ask!

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:02.000
You seem to have succeeded.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.630
Excuse me.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:13.850
Good evening.

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:23.140
The water's not bad.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.240
Yup.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:28.460
Did Itsuki tell you where he is?

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.830
He said he's at the outdoor bath.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.510
I see. Sorry to have bothered you.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.460
You seem to have failed.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:44.220
Outdoor bath, outdoor bath...

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.160
Found it.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.510
Uh, Suzuki-san?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.540
What is it?

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.430
Uh, I was wondering

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:03.180
what you meant the other day when 
you said you couldn't play with us.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.180
I meant exactly what I said.

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.240
Really?

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:10.820
It's no use. I don't understand.

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:15.540
Oh, right. I ditched Koa.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.320
Itsuki-kun.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.440
Huh? Rina-senpai?

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:25.520
Sorry. I finished the problem set.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.780
And I only logged in to talk to Kota.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:30.330
I haven't done any quests.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.220
Where are you right now?

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:36.150
At the outdoor bath...

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.470
Really? Are you alone?

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.510
What?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.520
Why?

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:47.760
<i>Does Rina-senpai know Suzuki-san is here?</i>

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.780
<i>No, she can't possibly...</i>

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:05.370
Rina-senpai, are you next door?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.370
I knew it.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:20.510
Has Itsuki-kun logged in yet?

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:28.020
Thanks for the problem set.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:31.270
I was surprised you finished it all.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.170
Once I started, I got pretty into it.

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.840
I was really able to focus.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:39.690
Just like when I first started playing <i>PSO2</i>.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.280
It'd be okay if you played some.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:44.280
What?

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:49.150
I said you couldn't play <i>PSO2</i> 
until the midterm exams,

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.540
but you can play a little.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.540
R-Really? All right!

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:58.670
Wha... Suzuki-san?

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.420
What? Suzuki-san?

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:02.180
Uh, nothing.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.810
What are you doing?

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.600
I-It flew out of the screen...

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.720
Last Samurai-san?

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.100
What happened?

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:17.360
A-A Darker

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:20.360
flew out of my screen...

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.770
A Darker?

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:26.990
Sheesh. That can't possibly have happened.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:28.840
No, it's true.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:31.170
It just flew out of the game.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:35.770
Then a girl came flying by, 
and the Darker ran away.

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:39.880
You were probably just drunk and dreaming.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:40.800
What?

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:44.180
Now that you mention it, 
maybe it was a dream.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.190
That aside...

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.100
You broke our promise.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.220
Yikes!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.160
<b>...would be nice, socially speaking. -> Satisfaction.</b>

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.550
Okay. Let's get to it.

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:26.900
Itsuki-kun.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.050
Rina-senpai?

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:32.150
Just because you got your grades back up,

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.630
doesn't mean you should be
playing <i>PSO2</i> in class.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.380
Actually, uh...

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:39.690
I'm studying and playing online 
games at the same time.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.940
Huh? Aren't you in class, too?

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:45.820
D-Don't worry about me.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:51.210
Izumi-san, could you answer the next problem?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:56.210
Yes. The text uses future tense, but...

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:02.150
That's all.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.510
Correct.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.210
Well done, Izumi-san.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:41.350
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.350 --> 00:24:09.210
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.440
The hot springs were nice.

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:46.480
A lot happened, but I'm glad I went.

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:48.690
Everyone should have friends.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:51.950
Speaking of hot springs, who were 
you in the outdoor bath with?

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:54.160
I heard you say "Suzuki-san."

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.370
Y-Yeah, right.

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:57.290
I was in the men's bath.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:58.620
I guess you're right.

00:23:58.620 --> 00:23:59.790
That's right.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.720
The outdoor bath was nice.

00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:04.140
I'd like to go back again, Tachibana Itsuki.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:04.870
Hey!

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:06.210
What does that mean?

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.210
It's not like that. It's not like that!
